# Heavy or regenerable artifacts of the portability lane.
#
# What is committed, and why:
#   ptx/            136 KB  -- the witness corpus. It IS the experiment, so it is
#                             committed even though gen_witnesses.py reproduces it.
#   out/*.tsv|json  small   -- every measured cell, so the matrix is auditable
#                             without re-running 15 min of x86 emulation.
#   out/triton/*.ptx        -- the PTX that proves the headline result (1024
#                             fma.rn.f32 on sm_75 where sm_80 has 16 mma.sync).
#                             Evidence, so committed.
#   out/tables.md           -- the generated tables on their own.

# upstream source tarballs: refetchable from codeload.github.com
subj/**/*.tar.gz

# the triton wheel cache (~149 MB); see src/README-images.md
wheels/

# per-cell cubins and disassembly: binary, large, and ptxas regenerates them
out/ladder_cubins/
out/cutlass/*.cubin
out/cutlass/*.cubin.sass
out/fa/*.cubin
out/fa/*.cubin.sass
out/selfval/

# the failed docker build recipe; superseded by `docker commit`, see
# src/README-images.md
Dockerfile.triton
